From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:21:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2279/3799] soh: rename func_80AB26DC ->
 EnNb_SetupConfrontationKneel

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: snaps to the cue's position and starts the collapse-to-kneeling animation with the kneeling draw mode
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Nb/z_en_nb.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Nb/z_en_nb.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Nb/z_en_nb.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Nb/z_en_nb.c
index d37635453..35a99f95f 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Nb/z_en_nb.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Nb/z_en_nb.c
@@ -764,7 +764,8 @@ void EnNb_SetupConfrontationHidden(EnNb* this) {
     this->actor.shape.shadowAlpha = 0;
 }
 
-void func_80AB26DC(EnNb* this, PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80AB26DC: snaps to the cue's position and starts the collapse-to-kneeling animation with the kneeling draw mode
+void EnNb_SetupConfrontationKneel(EnNb* this, PlayState* play) {
     s32 pad;
     AnimationHeader* animation = &gNabooruCollapseFromStandingToKneelingTransitionAnim;
     f32 lastFrame = Animation_GetLastFrame(animation);
@@ -874,7 +875,7 @@ void EnNb_CheckConfrontationCsMode(EnNb* this, PlayState* play) {
                     EnNb_SetupConfrontationHidden(this);  // was func_80AB26C8 [LLM:HIGH]
                     break;
                 case 10:
-                    func_80AB26DC(this, play);
+                    EnNb_SetupConfrontationKneel(this, play);  // was func_80AB26DC [LLM:HIGH]
                     break;
                 case 11:
                     EnNb_SetupKneel(this);
